    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d761">

                <pb facs="1043" n="923" sameAs="frus:frus1922v01/pg923"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">861.77/2781: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Great
                        Britain</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Harvey</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1922-10-26T18:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 26,
                                1922—6 p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>323. Department’s 312 via Paris.<anchor n="8" xml:id="d761-f1"/> French and
                    Japanese Governments have expressed concurrence in this Government’s proposal to
                        <pb facs="1044" n="924" xml:id="pg924"/> wind up Interallied Committee and
                    Technical Board on October 31st. Please draw matter to attention of Foreign
                    Office and endeavor to expedite its reply.</p>
                <p>Referring to Department’s 209, July 17, 3 p.m.,<anchor n="10" xml:id="d761-f2"/>
                    inform Foreign Office and repeat to Paris as Department’s No. 339, that
                    Department has just been advised of Italian Government’s concurrence in
                    proposals outlined in original memorandum.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Hughes</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d761-f1" n="8" xml:id="d761-f1-content">
                <p>See telegram no. 311, Oct. 13, to the Ambassador in France, with instructions to
                    repeat to London as no. 312, <ref target="#pg920">p. 920</ref>.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d761-f2" n="10" xml:id="d761-f2-content">
